{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on END a18e2cec: adopt the measured identifiers in this\nhead, then run a targeted follow-up. No full gate repeats.\n\n1. Run the three-package comparison once at `25f070a7`. Lending and\n   Counter are at the open 0.4.0, which changes freely by rule\n   163de663. Apply the measured presentation of each one. Entry,\n   definitions and semantic stay exact, and Grow stays byte-exact.\n   If one of those changes, stop and tell me.\n2. Commit the changed `release-identifiers.json` files in this\n   head. CB-1 carries them, because its change to\n   `version-questions.ts` is the cause.\n3. Follow-up, as in ruling 5fc60537: run the whole\n   `application-release-reproduction.test.ts` owner once. Then run\n   Plain and Native from the maintained stage descriptors, with the\n   natural Scale selection and unchanged workers and deadlines.\n   Node and Counting passed and do not repeat.\n4. Gate 1 stays FAIL in the record. The review request names the\n   failed gate, the identifier commit and the follow-up.\n5. A failure in the follow-up ends this route. The head then\n   repairs and runs one full gate. It keeps the slot in both cases.\n6. The four Page routes run after a passing follow-up.\n\nNew owner before a gate START: a head that changes a file under a\n`packages/*/src` directory, or the source of an example, runs the\nthree-package comparison first and states the result. It takes\nabout 3 s. Add the sentence to `docs/testing.md` in this head,\nbeside the two sentences of c637f63f and 5fc60537.\n\nThree pre-gate owners by rule is too many to remember. I file a\nrequest next that gives the gate one early stage for pinned values.\nIt takes no position before RS-1.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}